WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:03.274
Thank you so much for being here.

00:00:03.274 --> 00:00:05.672
People in Chicago love you.

00:00:05.672 --> 00:00:06.505
Love ya.

00:00:06.505 --> 00:00:07.580
Yeah, they're nice, they're nice.

00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:08.640
They're nice people here.

00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:09.473
They are wonderful people.

00:00:09.473 --> 00:00:10.621
You've got a wonderful state here.

00:00:10.621 --> 00:00:11.454
Absolutely.

00:00:11.454 --> 00:00:12.981
First of all, I wanna say...

00:00:12.981 --> 00:00:14.180
(laughing)

00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:17.060
I wanna say I'm a huge fan of your name.

00:00:17.060 --> 00:00:19.120
Your name, you have the best name.

00:00:19.120 --> 00:00:20.070
Barack Obama.

00:00:20.070 --> 00:00:22.270
When I first heard it, I
thought I was sure it was Irish,

00:00:22.270 --> 00:00:23.560
when I first heard it.

00:00:23.560 --> 00:00:24.450
It is...

00:00:24.450 --> 00:00:26.199
There's an apostrophe after the o.

00:00:26.199 --> 00:00:27.340
[Conan] I knew that, I knew that.

00:00:27.340 --> 00:00:29.780
And Barack is actually
an ancient Celtic name.

00:00:29.780 --> 00:00:30.870
Very nice.

00:00:30.870 --> 00:00:32.159
So we're ancient cousins,

00:00:32.159 --> 00:00:32.992
is what you're saying.
That's exactly right.

00:00:32.992 --> 00:00:34.010
You and me, we're right there.

00:00:34.010 --> 00:00:35.650
I'm taking you to Ireland someday.

00:00:35.650 --> 00:00:36.784
This is my brother here.

00:00:36.784 --> 00:00:38.210
(audience laughing)

00:00:38.210 --> 00:00:39.500
Now, there's a lot I have to ask you,

00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:42.320
first of all, you live in
Chicago, your wife is from here,

00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:43.520
any advice for me?

00:00:43.520 --> 00:00:45.400
I'm a guy, I don't know the area,

00:00:45.400 --> 00:00:46.880
what would you tell a guy?

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:48.160
Well, you know-

00:00:48.160 --> 00:00:48.993
[Conan] Where should I go?

00:00:48.993 --> 00:00:50.105
What should I do?

00:00:50.105 --> 00:00:50.938
The key is to get into the neighborhoods.

00:00:50.938 --> 00:00:52.610
You know, Millennium Park is beautiful,

00:00:52.610 --> 00:00:54.560
and Wrigley Field everybody knows about,

00:00:54.560 --> 00:00:58.165
but you know, going out
into the neighborhoods,

00:00:58.165 --> 00:01:00.020
visiting some local restaurants,

00:01:00.020 --> 00:01:01.810
for example, my favorite
restaurant in Chicago

00:01:01.810 --> 00:01:03.958
is a place on the west
side called MacArthur's.

00:01:03.958 --> 00:01:05.070
(audience cheering)

00:01:05.070 --> 00:01:06.518
Some folks know MacArthur's here.

00:01:06.518 --> 00:01:08.830
Some of the best soul food in Chicago.

00:01:08.830 --> 00:01:09.663
Soul food.

00:01:09.663 --> 00:01:12.265
And I mean, you'll stand out a little bit.

00:01:12.265 --> 00:01:14.667
(audience laughing)

00:01:14.667 --> 00:01:15.701
I will not.

00:01:15.701 --> 00:01:19.650
There aren't that many, six
six guys in the restaurant.

00:01:19.650 --> 00:01:22.910
It's about time they saw a
giant red pompadour in there.

00:01:22.910 --> 00:01:24.500
I want my soul food.

00:01:24.500 --> 00:01:25.991
Bring it on.

00:01:25.991 --> 00:01:29.230
Now, is it true that you've
gone to the same barbershop,

00:01:29.230 --> 00:01:31.283
is it true, here in Chicago, for 20 years?

00:01:31.283 --> 00:01:32.982
The Hyde Park Hair Salon.

00:01:32.982 --> 00:01:34.254
[Conan] Hyde Park Hair Salon.

00:01:34.254 --> 00:01:35.087
Hyde Park.

00:01:35.087 --> 00:01:35.930
Hyde Park?

00:01:35.930 --> 00:01:36.763
Okay.

00:01:36.763 --> 00:01:38.450
Do you tell people I'm
going to the barber shop

00:01:38.450 --> 00:01:39.897
or it's time for my
trip to the hair salon?

00:01:39.897 --> 00:01:41.740
No, no, the...

00:01:41.740 --> 00:01:44.512
It's called hair salon,
but when you go in there,

00:01:44.512 --> 00:01:46.910
it's more shop than salon.

00:01:46.910 --> 00:01:47.743
Right?

00:01:47.743 --> 00:01:48.980
And it sounds like a nice
kinda down to earth place,

00:01:48.980 --> 00:01:50.360
not too fussy.

00:01:50.360 --> 00:01:51.546
You know, you sit down...

00:01:51.546 --> 00:01:54.890
The first time I went there
was with a guy named Wally.

00:01:54.890 --> 00:01:56.182
He's an old grumpy guy.

00:01:56.182 --> 00:01:58.275
And he's day, "Sit
down, what do you want?"

00:01:58.275 --> 00:02:00.190
And I'd say, "Well, I'm not sure."

00:02:00.190 --> 00:02:01.750
Okay, just shut up.

00:02:01.750 --> 00:02:03.599
And he'd start cutting your hair.

00:02:03.599 --> 00:02:06.525
That's a great service
technique, just shut up.

00:02:06.525 --> 00:02:09.192
But now I've got a guy who's...

00:02:09.192 --> 00:02:12.513
He and I, we've been
together for about 10 years.

00:02:14.410 --> 00:02:16.880
Very brave of you to come out with this.

00:02:16.880 --> 00:02:19.990
Listen, let me say, the
relationship between

00:02:19.990 --> 00:02:22.182
a man and his barber, that's...

00:02:22.182 --> 00:02:24.240
It's sacred, it's a real bond.

00:02:24.240 --> 00:02:25.073
It's serious business.

00:02:25.073 --> 00:02:26.170
Where do you get your hair cut, Conan?

00:02:26.170 --> 00:02:27.340
I don't, this isn't real.

00:02:27.340 --> 00:02:29.410
This is, scientists work on this.

00:02:29.410 --> 00:02:31.490
(audience applause)

00:02:31.490 --> 00:02:34.103
This is a high density
polymer that NASA invented.

00:02:35.880 --> 00:02:36.713
Hair.

00:02:36.713 --> 00:02:38.430
Hair is for wimps.

00:02:38.430 --> 00:02:41.229
This has robotics in it, it can do things.

00:02:41.229 --> 00:02:42.710
Ah, there you go.

00:02:42.710 --> 00:02:45.710
(audience laughing)

00:02:47.140 --> 00:02:48.720
I'm an ass, by the way.

00:02:48.720 --> 00:02:50.710
I wanna talk about something.

00:02:50.710 --> 00:02:54.510
First time that you had real
intense national exposure,

00:02:54.510 --> 00:02:55.343
and the first time I think you came to

00:02:55.343 --> 00:02:56.550
a lot of people's attention,

00:02:56.550 --> 00:02:58.990
2004 democratic national convention,

00:02:58.990 --> 00:03:00.700
you gave the keynote address.

00:03:00.700 --> 00:03:01.970
You blew everybody away.

00:03:01.970 --> 00:03:04.558
People are still talking
about that speech.

00:03:04.558 --> 00:03:05.851
Brilliant speech.
(audience applause)

00:03:05.851 --> 00:03:06.851
Thank you.

00:03:08.155 --> 00:03:11.590
And I was thinking, do you ever use...

00:03:11.590 --> 00:03:13.700
You have such oratorical
power, have you ever,

00:03:13.700 --> 00:03:15.860
do you ever go home to your family

00:03:15.860 --> 00:03:18.755
and try and use that oratorical power?

00:03:18.755 --> 00:03:20.951
I'll tell you a quick story.

00:03:20.951 --> 00:03:22.802
You know, we have dinner together,

00:03:22.802 --> 00:03:25.371
my wife asked my two
daughters, seven and four,

00:03:25.371 --> 00:03:27.260
Malia, how was your day?

00:03:27.260 --> 00:03:28.826
She'll say, "Tell us about it."

00:03:28.826 --> 00:03:31.199
Four year old, Sasha, how was your day?

00:03:31.199 --> 00:03:33.280
They ask my wife, how's your day?

00:03:33.280 --> 00:03:34.397
Then finally, my wife says,

00:03:34.397 --> 00:03:37.170
"Well, let's ask daddy how his day was."

00:03:37.170 --> 00:03:40.887
And my four year old will say, "Boring."

00:03:42.819 --> 00:03:46.320
And my wife will say,
"Well, that's not nice.

00:03:46.320 --> 00:03:49.580
You know, actually, people come
and listen to daddy speak."

00:03:49.580 --> 00:03:51.380
And the two of them fall
out of their chairs.

00:03:51.380 --> 00:03:53.826
They think that is the funniest thing.

00:03:53.826 --> 00:03:56.250
The notion that somebody
would be interested

00:03:56.250 --> 00:03:58.410
in what their father has to say.

00:03:58.410 --> 00:03:59.720
Kids just don't care, yeah.

00:03:59.720 --> 00:04:01.290
But have you ever been tempted to just

00:04:01.290 --> 00:04:03.280
jump up behind a podium
in front of your kids

00:04:03.280 --> 00:04:05.483
to tell them, you know, go to your room?

00:04:06.983 --> 00:04:09.190
Using the great Barack Obama voice.

00:04:09.190 --> 00:04:10.677
My fellow Obamas.

00:04:11.769 --> 00:04:13.269
The time has come.

00:04:14.810 --> 00:04:16.110
I'll try that out.

00:04:16.110 --> 00:04:18.063
That would work for you.

00:04:18.063 --> 00:04:20.783
You will clean your room in this century.

00:04:21.901 --> 00:04:24.430
Have you always been a gifted speaker?

00:04:24.430 --> 00:04:25.847
Have you always...
No, no.

00:04:25.847 --> 00:04:26.750
Was it something that
you developed over time?

00:04:26.750 --> 00:04:29.360
No, you know, I have
flopped so many times.

00:04:29.360 --> 00:04:31.140
I think it's like being a comic, you know,

00:04:31.140 --> 00:04:33.322
you get up and every...

00:04:33.322 --> 00:04:36.347
And sometimes it's working for you,

00:04:36.347 --> 00:04:38.604
but you know that time
where everybody just--

00:04:38.604 --> 00:04:41.320
I don't know what you're talking about.

00:04:41.320 --> 00:04:44.808
You start getting kind
of hot flashes and...

00:04:44.808 --> 00:04:45.641
No.

00:04:45.641 --> 00:04:46.474
No?

00:04:46.474 --> 00:04:47.413
(laughing)

00:04:47.413 --> 00:04:48.246
Yeah, yeah.

00:04:48.246 --> 00:04:49.079
Is this one of those moments?

00:04:49.079 --> 00:04:49.912
No, no, no.

00:04:49.912 --> 00:04:50.790
I know exactly what you're talking about.

00:04:50.790 --> 00:04:51.760
Anyone who's a...

00:04:51.760 --> 00:04:53.360
And so how do you handle when you...

00:04:53.360 --> 00:04:55.590
Because people, I think, just assume that

00:04:55.590 --> 00:04:57.350
you're such a gifted speaker,

00:04:57.350 --> 00:04:58.680
that you've never had those moments.

00:04:58.680 --> 00:05:00.460
Describe what it's like for
you when you're up there

00:05:00.460 --> 00:05:02.920
and you feel like it's not
working, you're not getting them.

00:05:02.920 --> 00:05:05.130
It's not working, and the
main mistake everybody makes,

00:05:05.130 --> 00:05:07.713
and I do the same thing, is you
just keep on talking, right?

00:05:07.713 --> 00:05:09.410
' Cause you think, well,
eventually I'm gonna

00:05:09.410 --> 00:05:10.740
come up with something that they like,

00:05:10.740 --> 00:05:14.521
and that makes it worse
because what happens is

00:05:14.521 --> 00:05:16.920
not only are you bad,
but you're long winded.

00:05:16.920 --> 00:05:18.146
Right, right.

00:05:18.146 --> 00:05:21.730
Do you just throw out random
words at a certain point?

00:05:21.730 --> 00:05:24.363
Corndog, onion, blueberry.

00:05:25.205 --> 00:05:26.320
Anything here, people?

00:05:26.320 --> 00:05:28.281
Yeah, yeah.

00:05:28.281 --> 00:05:30.490
But I think that's what's been happening

00:05:30.490 --> 00:05:32.173
in the White House lately.

00:05:32.173 --> 00:05:36.090
(audience cheers and applause)

00:05:44.091 --> 00:05:47.160
Throw anything against the refrigerator,

00:05:47.160 --> 00:05:47.993
see if it sticks.

00:05:47.993 --> 00:05:48.826
Yeah.

00:05:48.826 --> 00:05:50.091
Well, let me ask you something.

00:05:50.091 --> 00:05:51.740
I know president Bush
is famous for nicknames.

00:05:51.740 --> 00:05:53.560
Has he tried to give you a nickname?

00:05:53.560 --> 00:05:55.030
He loves to give everybody...

00:05:55.030 --> 00:05:56.350
You know, the thing...

00:05:56.350 --> 00:05:59.050
I can't tell whether he's
trying to give me a nickname

00:05:59.050 --> 00:06:00.879
or whether he just
can't pronounce my name.

00:06:00.879 --> 00:06:03.879
(audience laughing)

00:06:05.910 --> 00:06:09.355
[Conan] Give him the benefit of the doubt.

00:06:09.355 --> 00:06:11.652
Sometimes he calls me Bama.

00:06:11.652 --> 00:06:12.485
[Conan] Bama?

00:06:12.485 --> 00:06:13.318
Bama.

00:06:13.318 --> 00:06:14.909
Sometimes he calls me Rock.

00:06:14.909 --> 00:06:16.160
He calls you what?

00:06:16.160 --> 00:06:16.993
Rock.

00:06:16.993 --> 00:06:17.826
Rock.

00:06:17.826 --> 00:06:18.821
Rock is cool.

00:06:18.821 --> 00:06:19.654
Rock is not bad.

00:06:19.654 --> 00:06:20.487
Bama, Rock.

00:06:20.487 --> 00:06:21.320
I like that, yeah.

00:06:21.320 --> 00:06:22.153
Yeah.

00:06:22.153 --> 00:06:23.600
(laughing)

00:06:23.600 --> 00:06:25.050
I just picture him going Bama.

00:06:25.050 --> 00:06:27.127
Get Bama, get Bama, get Rock.

00:06:27.127 --> 00:06:28.410
Mr President, are you all right?

00:06:28.410 --> 00:06:30.503
They're gonna think he's
having a fit or something.

00:06:31.440 --> 00:06:34.140
Now, I'm curious, you
have been very successful,

00:06:34.140 --> 00:06:37.200
you've had a lot of success
and a lot of adulation.

00:06:37.200 --> 00:06:38.400
You've been very successful, I think,

00:06:38.400 --> 00:06:40.240
at remaining humble and
having a sense of humor

00:06:40.240 --> 00:06:41.073
about yourself.

00:06:41.073 --> 00:06:43.483
Does that come naturally to you?

00:06:43.483 --> 00:06:44.410
It's my wife.

00:06:44.410 --> 00:06:45.460
It's your wife.

00:06:45.460 --> 00:06:47.420
It's nice when someone
else does it for you.

00:06:47.420 --> 00:06:48.579
Yeah, exactly.

00:06:48.579 --> 00:06:51.130
She tells me about my ears.

00:06:51.130 --> 00:06:52.300
She talks about my ears a lot.

00:06:52.300 --> 00:06:54.490
That's an old standard, how big they are.

00:06:54.490 --> 00:06:55.323
Oh really?

00:06:55.323 --> 00:06:56.156
That's nice.

00:06:56.156 --> 00:06:57.090
So your kids are saying boring

00:06:57.090 --> 00:06:58.740
and she's like, "Yeah, big ears."

00:07:00.229 --> 00:07:02.400
This is a horrible home life you have.

00:07:02.400 --> 00:07:04.660
It's basically, you know...

00:07:05.844 --> 00:07:08.998
Often I come home feeling
pretty full of myself

00:07:08.998 --> 00:07:11.040
and they knock me down pretty quick.

00:07:11.040 --> 00:07:11.873
Yeah.

00:07:11.873 --> 00:07:14.325
I think that's what
our loved ones are for.

00:07:14.325 --> 00:07:15.320
That's why we marry.

00:07:15.320 --> 00:07:16.743
I feel good, oh yeah?

00:07:18.920 --> 00:07:19.933
Thanks mom.

00:07:22.261 --> 00:07:24.990
Now I have to ask you, I
wouldn't be doing my job,

00:07:24.990 --> 00:07:26.822
that's not true, I'm a
comedian, not a pundit,

00:07:26.822 --> 00:07:28.450
but I'm gonna ask anyway.

00:07:28.450 --> 00:07:29.980
So many people are speculating,

00:07:29.980 --> 00:07:31.770
you hear Barack Obama is gonna be

00:07:31.770 --> 00:07:32.880
a presidential candidate in '08

00:07:32.880 --> 00:07:34.430
or he's gonna be on the ticket.

00:07:35.295 --> 00:07:37.540
And I just wanna say...
(audience applause)

00:07:37.540 --> 00:07:39.219
I just wanna say,

00:07:39.219 --> 00:07:41.440
if there's something
you'd like to say here,

00:07:41.440 --> 00:07:44.090
there's probably never a
better venue than right now.

00:07:47.976 --> 00:07:49.940
This is the kind of thing you wanna say

00:07:49.940 --> 00:07:52.321
just after Chewbacca has
made out with George Wayne.

00:07:52.321 --> 00:07:54.976
(laughing)

00:07:54.976 --> 00:07:57.865
I was thinking about
you as my running mate.

00:07:57.865 --> 00:07:58.698
Oh, hey.

00:07:58.698 --> 00:08:01.531
(audience cheers)

00:08:02.391 --> 00:08:03.224
Me and Conan.

00:08:04.486 --> 00:08:07.029
It sounds good, Obama O'Brien.

00:08:07.029 --> 00:08:10.170
Obama O'Brien sounds amazing, yeah.

00:08:10.170 --> 00:08:11.253
Obama O'Brien.

00:08:11.253 --> 00:08:13.553
It would be the worst thing you ever did.

00:08:14.448 --> 00:08:17.060
You'd think it was funny
and then like a day later

00:08:17.060 --> 00:08:19.375
you'd be like, this guy is an idiot.

00:08:19.375 --> 00:08:21.393
Barack, come on over, let's talk.

00:08:25.045 --> 00:08:27.100
It's been a thrilling week for us,

00:08:27.100 --> 00:08:29.690
but it was a real honor to have you be on

00:08:29.690 --> 00:08:31.090
our last show here in Chicago.

00:08:31.090 --> 00:08:32.430
And I know you're a busy person,

00:08:32.430 --> 00:08:34.400
but we were thrilled when
you said you'd stop by.

00:08:34.400 --> 00:08:37.700
Listen, I love Conan
O'Brien and most of all,

00:08:37.700 --> 00:08:38.865
I love the audience here.

00:08:38.865 --> 00:08:41.030
(audience cheers and applause)

00:08:41.030 --> 00:08:41.863
The guy's a pro.

00:08:41.863 --> 00:08:44.555
Thank you so much, Senator Barack Obama.

00:08:44.555 --> 00:08:47.138
Coming up, we'll be right back.

